{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"a9181ea5-4925-4671-ab07-79e5a89cba0a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The second publish failed because the **similarity score** was being stored as a Python `float`. DynamoDB rejects native floats and requires `Decimal` (or integer) types. On the first publish the table was empty, so no scores were written and the write succeeded; on any subsequent publish a score is present, triggering the `TypeError`.\n\n### Fix applied\n1. **Imported `Decimal`** and converted each similarity score before adding it to the DynamoDB item.  \n2. Updated the `related` function to store the score as `Decimal(str(...))`.\n\n```python\n# src/app.py\nfrom decimal import Decimal   # \u003c-- new import\n\n...\nscored.append({\n    \"slug\": other[\"slug\"],\n    \"score\": Decimal(str(similarity(story, other)))   # \u003c-- conversion\n})\n```\n\n### What from the colleague’s note was relevant\n- **State‑dependent bug** – the error only appears after the table has data.  \n- **Root cause** – using Python floats in a DynamoDB `put_item`.  \n- **Single‑line fix** – converting the score to a Dynamo‑compatible type (`Decimal`).  \n- **Testing insight** – seeding the table before testing would have revealed the bug.\n\nBoth the first and subsequent publishes now succeed.\n\n**Reference files**\n- Updated source: [src/app.py](file:///tmp/h-IAGN6w/src/app.py)  \n- Explanation \u0026 fix details: [ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/a9181ea5-4925-4671-ab07-79e5a89cba0a/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":32.986437,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":13093,"output_tokens":2586,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":103360,"total_tokens":15679}}}
